<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramesses III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">assassinated c. 1153 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century-bce">12th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramesses III was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/twentieth-dynasty-of-egypt">Twentieth Dynasty</a> of the Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>. He defeated land and sea invasions by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-peoples">Sea Peoples</a> around 1177 BCE, preserving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> during the Late Bronze Age collapse. He was assassinated in a harem conspiracy around 1153 BCE, after which the New Kingdom declined under a series of weak successors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramesses-iii.jpg" alt="Ramesses III" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Asavaa · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KhonsuTemple-Karnak-RamessesIII-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
